  "markdown": "# RAQIB weekly operations report \u2014 raqib_demo_store\n\nPeriod 2026-08-29 to 2026-09-05 \u00b7 generated 2026-09-05T20:40 UTC\n\n## 1. Three measured results\n- Service level (share of 15-min slots with queue \u2264 3): **99.4%** (target 90%)\n- Store on-shelf availability: **97.7%**; footfall 4425 customers, 26.3 per hour\n- Peak checkout utilisation \u03c1: **0.95** with 3 tills available\n\n## 2. Queue model vs observed\n| Slot (UTC) | \u03bb /h | \u03bc /h per till | \u03c1 | W_q model (min) | W_q observed (min) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 18:00 | 52 | 41 | 0.43 | 0.1 | - |\n| 18:15 | 64 | 37 | 0.57 | 0.4 | - |\n| 18:30 | 72 | 39 | 0.62 | 0.5 | - |\n| 18:45 | 56 | 36 | 0.52 | 0.3 | - |\n| 19:00 | 68 | 41 | 0.55 | 0.3 | - |\n| 19:15 | 104 | 36 | 0.95 | 10.3 | 5.8 |\n| 19:30 | 72 | 38 | 0.64 | 0.6 | - |\n| 19:45 | 96 | 41 | 0.77 | 1.3 | - |\n\u03bc is estimated from video dwell times, not POS. Observed W_q uses Little's law on the measured queue length.\n\n## 3. Forecast vs seasonal naive\nNext-24h footfall model MAE **4.341** vs seasonal-naive **4.917** (11.7% better). Peaks expected at 21:00, 11:00, 12:00 UTC.\n\n## 4. Workforce plan (MILP, \u03c1 \u2264 0.85)\nPlanned staff-hours **184.0** vs **313.5** with today's 3 tills open all week (saves 129.5 h). Peak 4 tills, mean 1.76; 3 slots need more than the 3 tills open today.\nBefore/after simulation: customer wait 1583.2 \u2192 1310.6 customer-minutes per day (**17.2% reduction**).\n\n## 5. Recommended actions\n1. **Open 4 tills at the evening peak** \u2014 peak arrival rate 104/h drives utilisation 0.68 at the planned tills; the MILP plan uses 184.0 staff-hours vs 313.5 flat. Expected: 17% less customer wait time (1583 to 1311 customer-minutes/day).\n2. **Move shelf B3 to a 30-minute replenishment check** \u2014 on-shelf availability 97.3% this week, mean time to restock 38 min. Expected: raise OSA on B3 toward the 98% target by cutting gap episodes roughly in half.\n3. **Pre-position one floater before forecast peaks** \u2014 next-24h footfall forecast peaks at 21:00, 11:00, 12:00 UTC; model MAE 4.341 vs seasonal naive 4.917 (11.7% better). Expected: avoid the first 5 minutes of queue build-up at each peak, worth about one severity-2 queue alert per peak.\n\n## 6. Agent governance\n1 agent actions (1 autonomous, 0 proposals, human approval rate -), 1 tool calls, 0 failed, model cost $0.0.\n\n## 7. Data quality\nSimulated share of events: 100.0%. Service rate source: estimated_from_video. Faces are blurred at capture; no identity data exists in this report."
